  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b,\\) define \\(a \\$ b = (a - b)^2.\\) What is \\((x - y)^2 \\$ (y - x)^2?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x^2 + y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2x^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(4xy\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "0"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2008-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\((y - x)^2 = (x - y)^2,\\) both inputs to the operation are the same value \\(t = (x - y)^2.\\)\n\nTherefore \\((x - y)^2 \\$ (y - x)^2\\) \\(= t \\$ t\\) \\(= (t - t)^2 = 0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Note that \\((y - x)^2 = (x - y)^2\\)",
        "So the expression is \\(t \\$ t\\) with \\(t = (x - y)^2,\\) and \\(t \\$ t = (t - t)^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
